te-limits-hit-100-with-no-use-renewal-date-gets-postponed-every-day/1365569)\nciteturn2379search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 10 months ago; simone.m.romeo November 8, 2025, 5:29am 1 ... I haven’t been able to use codex for a week, filed complains to support@openai.com, contacted the staff on X, but no reply.\n\n# Codex Rate Limits hit 100% with no use. Renewal date get's postponed every day\n\nCodex\n\ncodex\n\nsimone.m.romeo November 8, 2025, 5:29am 1\n\nI use Codex through my Plus account in the IDEs extensions (Cursor and VS Code).\n\nIn the night between Friday and Saturday one week ago, my Codex weekly rate limit jumped from 88% to 100% during the night.\n\nWhat’s worse, the renewal date gets postponed every day even if I am not able to use codex (two days ago it said it would renew on Nov 13, yesterday it was Nov 14, today it says Nov 15). I haven’t been able to use codex for a week, filed complains to support@openai.com, contacted the staff on X, but no reply.\n\nIs the only option just leave Codex? Any suggestion what I may do?\n\nEDIT:\n\nI realized I’m an idiot. There was no limit. Just the way credits showed has been changed. It used to show how many credits I had used. Now it’s showing how many credits I have left. This made me think I couldn’t use codex anymore. But it’s no issue anymore.\n\nmedian-fridges November 8, 2025, 2:11pm 2\n\nCodex now totally useful, unfortunately.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChatKit Client Tool callback issue - API - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/chatkit-client-tool-callback-issue/1365626)\nciteturn2379search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 10 months ago; a5hpip3 November 8, 2025, 7:01pm 1 ... If anyone has found a workaround or receives updates from the OpenAI team, please share here or on the issue.\nOpenAI Developer Community\n\n# ChatKit Client Tool callback issue\n\nAPI\n\nagent-builder, chatkit\n\na5hpip3 November 8, 2025, 7:01pm 1\n\nHello all - I’m prototyping an agent work flow in agent builder UI, have a hosted ChatKit instance running on my app. The workflow is working great until it gets to the agent node that calls the ClientTool function to render content on the UI. The function is invoked correctly by the agent, and content renders on the UI, but then my workflow doesn’t proceed to the next node. It seems to be stuck in a loop on the render node. When i try in playground, I get the same result - the workflow gets to the rendering node, calls the function to render on the front end, but then is expecting a response - when I send a success response, it just re-runs the same render node; stuck in loop.\n\nThe agent config is as follows -\n#######\nInstructions:\nYour job is to compile content, call a client tool call and render the compiled content on the UI. After receiving confirmation of successful tool call, always:\n\n  * Acknowledge that you’ve created the module\n  * Offer to create additional modules\n\nAfter calling render_to_canvas and receiving confirmation, always:\n\n  * Acknowledge that you’ve created the module\n  * Offer to create additional modules\n\nThe client tool to call is: [render_to_canvas]\n\nUser message:\nCall the client tool [render_to_canvas] to render. content from {{workflow.input_as_text}}\n#######\n\nIt seems from docs that there are lower level parameters that can be configured in the SDK. Since I’m prototyping I’m using the hosted instance for speed. Figured this would be basic functionality that should just work right of the box. I feel like I’m doing something wrong here - anyone come across this issue? Or if you’ve done function calls in the past on agents, is there an expected response structure that I need to follow?\n\nAppreciate any insight on this!\n\nh6503 November 9, 2025, 10:15pm 2\n\nI have the same problem too\n\nh6503 November 10, 2025, 7:02pm 3\n\nI fix it by turning on conversation history and chat history.\n\ni dont if it is the case for you but definitely turning them off will cause these errors\n\na5hpip3 November 11, 2025, 1:00am 4\n\nI had history on - but anyway I created another end agent node that renders using client tools - chat history on. Also on the client side, returning just a plain {} seems to also help since my agent isn’t looking for data to be returned.\n\nh6503 November 13, 2025, 3:58am 5\n\nit completely broken as of today, cannot call any client tool anymore\n\nsbarman25 November 13, 2025, 5:28am 6\n\nJust checked, client tool isn’t working.\n\nwitek November 13, 2025, 6:30am 7\n\nTool calling is not working for us as well Image: :confused: it is already few hours\n\nPaulo_Coronado November 13, 2025, 11:25am 8\n\nAlso experiencing onClientTool issue. My `onClientTool` handler executes successfully and returns a valid JSON object, but the agent immediately breaks after that.\n\nThe client tool runs correctly, but ChatKit can’t send the result back to the agent.\n\nPS.: I am using `@openai/chatkit-react` with Agent Builder client tools.\n\nPaulo_Coronado November 13, 2025, 11:44am 9\n\nI’ve created an issue in the official ChatKit Github repo to track this problem: /openai/chatkit-js/issues/94.\n\nIf anyone has found a workaround or receives updates from the OpenAI team, please share here or on the issue. Thanks!\n\nwilkes November 13, 2025, 4:46pm 10\n\nHi all, we’re investigating this issue. Thanks for your patience in the mean time.\n\nwilkes November 13, 2025, 5:37pm 11\n\nWe identified the issue have rolled it back. Error rates for client side tool calls look to have dropped down to about 0\n\na5hpip3 November 15, 2025, 4:39pm 12\n\nMy client tools function call is rendering on the UI, but it is not very reliable. Often it fails silently which is frustrating because if there was any server side update we could invoke a retry action. Is there some best practices guide on how to work with client tools for UI rendering? I want to make sure I’m structuring the output and response correctly. At this point the reliability is so low that I’m considering not using client tools at all and instead persisting in db and fetching to render.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProblem syncing GitHub with ChatGPT (“There was a problem syncing GitHub. Try again later.”) - Codex CLI - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/problem-syncing-github-with-chatgpt-there-was-a-problem-syncing-github-try-again-later/1365594)\nciteturn2379search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; Cernunnos November 8, 2025, 11:08am 1\n\n# Problem syncing GitHub with ChatGPT (“There was a problem syncing GitHub. Try again later.”)\n\nCodex Codex CLI\n\nCernunnos November 8, 2025, 11:08am 1\n\nHi,\n\nI’m having persistent issues connecting my GitHub account to ChatGPT. Each time I try to sync my repositories, I get the following error message at the top of the screen:\n\n“There was a problem syncing GitHub. Try again later.”\n\nI’ve already tried the following troubleshooting steps, but the problem persists:\n\nDisconnected and reconnected my GitHub account multiple times.\n\nUsed an incognito/private browser window.\n\nCleared browser cache and cookies.\n\nTried from different browsers (Chrome, Firefox).\n\nVerified that ChatGPT appears in my Authorized OAuth Apps on GitHub with full repo and read:user permissions.\n\nChecked my network and GitHub security logs — no indication of a block.\n\nDespite that, I still see the error, and the sync never completes.\nThe repositories do appear in the selection list, but ChatGPT fails right after I click Continue.\n\nCould you please check if there’s an issue with the GitHub integration on your side and what could be done?\n\nThanks a lot for your help.\n\nandrew70 November 10, 2025, 11:48am 4\n\nSame issue here. GitHub is seemingly connected, but repos syncing is not working. Seeing an error “There was a problem syncing GitHub. Try again later.” I can still select repos from “company knowledge” tab, though and I see them connected in Codex. But I guess automatic syncing will make it work faster and more conext will be available to GPT. Pls fix it. GitHub support says it’s on GPT’s side.\n\nExotic November 11, 2025, 3:08am 5\n\nseeing the same issue with ChatGPT pro\n\ntried disconnecting and reconnecting my github but the issue still persists\n\nshadvick November 12, 2025, 10:01pm 6\n\nalso trying to connect chatgpt to github and get the error “There was a problem syncing GitHub. Try again later.”\n\n92slawa92 November 13, 2025, 6:08am 7\n\nSame problem since October, when something being wrong with cloud storage worldwide--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKruel.ai KV2.0 - KX (experimental research) to current 8.2- Api companion co-pilot system with full modality , understanding with persistent memory - #450 by darcschnider - Community - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/kruel-ai-kv2-0-kx-experimental-research-to-current-8-2-api-companion-co-pilot-system-with-full-modality-understanding-with-persistent-memory/674592/450)\nciteturn2379search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 9 months ago; darcschnider November 8, 2025, 9:48am 450\n\ndarcschnider November 8, 2025, 9:48am 450\n\n# Shipping Notes: Web Frontend for V8.2, Mobile UX, and Performance Gains\n\nI started early this morning (3:00 a.m.) to wrap a lingering debug item and finalize work from yesterday’s build cycle. While part of the team handled other software tasks, our AIs continued provisioning and validating the new server builds in parallel. Below is a concise update on what shipped, what changed, and what’s next.\n\n## What We Shipped\n\n### Web Frontend for V8.2\n\n  * Context: V8.2 has been a desktop-first client. To support cloud accessibility and a wider range of devices, we built a dedicated web frontend.\n\n  * Mobile-first scope: We focused on features that make sense on a smartphone: fast load, minimal taps, and responsive layouts.\n\n  * Voice input change: We removed Whisper on the web; modern mobile keyboards already offer reliable microphone input, which is sufficient for short prompts and messages.\n\n### Personal Creation & Editor\n\n  * We exposed the persona/entity creation and editor directly in the UI. This should always be available to users for constructing and refining entities, preferences, and roles without engineering support.\n\n### Music Deck (Web)\n\n  * We introduced a lightweight music deck for web that lists your generated tracks and supports background play (you can close the deck and keep listening).\n\n  * Planned enhancement: Implement automatic ducking—when TTS is speaking, the music volume lowers, then returns to its previous level.\n\n## Platform & Infrastructure\n\n### File Upload Pipeline (Vision + Docs)\n\n  * File upload is core to vision and document understanding. We’re finalizing a more robust path that avoids port conflicts introduced by locally bound models.\n\n  * Action: We’re moving local model services into Docker to align ports within the Docker network and eliminate external bindings. This simplifies deployment, reduces conflicts, and keeps networking contained.\n\n## Performance Snapshot\n\nWe’ve been tuning steadily, and current end-to-end response times are competitive with fast mid-reasoning stacks:\n\n  * Typical latency: ~10–28 seconds, depending on data volume and context breadth.\n\n  * Example: Querying across one month of data can take ~28 seconds, influenced by topic complexity, linked historical context, and the density of related discussions.\n\n## Hardware Notes\n\nOur compact GPU workstation (“DGX Spark” in our lab notes) continues to punch above its weight for a dev lab. The experience has been compelling enough that the next step is a DGX Station–class upgrade to scale concurrent workloads and multi-user throughput.\n\n## What’s Next: P2P Alpha & Research Protocol\n\nWe’re preparing peer-to-peer testing with a small group of trusted Alpha members. This will be a research-style rollout:\n\n  * Deliberate pace: We’ll prioritize careful observation over speed.\n\n  * Deep telemetry: We’ll analyze logs, model behavior, and user journaling to understand how models grow, where friction occurs, and how memory evolves across sessions and contexts.\n\n  * Goal: Validate that kruel.ai consistently “understands the now” and—more importantly—understands the user. The aim is a system that feels like a capable partner: context-aware, persistent, and responsive to personal workflows.\n\n## Why This Matters\n\nLarge chat systems are incredible, but they’re often constrained by session boundaries and fragmented memory. Our approach is a memex-style architecture: no “amnesia” between sessions, and a unified memory that tracks entities, timelines, and relationships over time. That continuity is what makes kruel.ai feel closer to a proto-companion—something that learns your patterns and collaborates with you across days, weeks, and projects.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCompatibility Issues with Desktop App on Mac - #36 by BriggsMonty - ChatGPT - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/compatibility-issues-with-desktop-app-on-mac/765557/36)\nciteturn2379search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; BriggsMonty November 8, 2025, 4:21am 36\n\n# Compatibility Issues with Desktop App on Mac\n\nChatGPT\n\nBriggsMonty November 8, 2025, 4:21am 36\n\never since my mother got a new MacBook I inherited her old MacBook Pro. I don’t know the exact specs and year cuz this is the first Mac I have ever had(I do know its intel based and it has a Touch Bar-love those things). But I can say I like it a lot. Of course the $2000 windows pc I built is a lot better at running games and really anything without breaking a sweat. Calling Mac users “idiots” would’ve been me a couple weeks ago-maybe even days. but this os was so easy to get used to though I thought it was going to be a lot harder. I too was very team windows but now that I have a decent MacBook and a beast of a pc. i like both a lot…. also I enjoy apple arcade gam es but I’m still not fully used to the whole Mac setup so I use a thunderbolt 4 cable to connect the Mac to my thunderbolt 4 add in card on my pc and I create a thunderbolt bridge so I can connect to the Mac remotely over the wired network and have 0 latency over Parsec, Tightvnc, you name it… anyway I don’t appreciate how you call Mac user idiots just because you think the os is inferior. From a lifetime windows user, I like it a lot..--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBatch API - connection error for large files - Bugs - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/batch-api-connection-error-for-large-files/1364647)\nciteturn2379search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 11 months ago; Initial connection succeeds (HTTP 200 OK) but drops partway through transfer, suggesting a timeout or streaming issue on OpenAI’s infrastructure. ... Partha_Chakraborty November 8, 2025, 1:28am 2\n\n# Batch API - connection error for large files\n\nAPI Bugs\n\napi, batch-api\n\nfspah October 31, 2025, 10:12pm 1\n\nI cannot download large batch output files (>100MB) when trying to retrieve batch processing results via the Files API. Downloads consistently fail mid-transfer with connection errors.\n\nTimeline: This worked fine a few weeks ago, but has been failing consistently for several days now.\n\nDetails:\n\n  * File size: 242 MB\n\n  * Error: Connection drops after 10-30 MB downloaded\n\n  * Small files (<10MB): Download successfully\n\n  * Large files (>100MB): Consistently fail\n\nErrors encountered:\n\n  * `APIConnectionError: Connection error`\n\n  * `504 Gateway Time-out`\n\n  * `HTTP/2 stream error: INTERNAL_ERROR`\n\nAttempted workarounds:\n\n  * OpenAI Python SDK with various settings\n\n  * Chunked downloads with HTTP Range headers → results in corrupted data with duplicate truncated lines\n\n  * curl with retry logic and HTTP/1.1\n\n  * Different networks/VPN\n\nInitial connection succeeds (HTTP 200 OK) but drops partway through transfer, suggesting a timeout or streaming issue on OpenAI’s infrastructure.\n\nHas anyone else experienced this? Is there a known workaround, or is this an OpenAI infrastructure issue that needs to be addressed?\n\nPartha_Chakraborty November 8, 2025, 1:28am 2\n\nFacing the same issue. Have you found a solution?--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLatest topics - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/latest?no_definitions=true&order=likes&page=1203)\nciteturn2379search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Vector stores not being attached assistants when creating threads Bugs assistants ,  assistants-api ,  assistants-files ,  vector-store  |  | 1  | 159  | November 8, 2025 ... Migrating from Responses + OpenAI Vector Stores to my own RAG Tool with Agents: looking for feedback on tool design API agents ,  tools ,  agents-sdk ,  responses-api  |  | 0  | 134  | November 6, 2025\nOpenAI Developer Community\n\nTopic  |  | Replies  | Views  | Activity\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nCodex as an Autonomous Engineer: Refactoring OpenStack’s Front End into a Unified Streamlit Console Use cases and examples codex ,  codex-cli ,  gpt-5-codex ,  codex-cloud  |  | 1  | 261  | September 8, 2026\nGrouping Option in ChatGPT Atlas Feature requests atlas  |  | 0  | 45  | November 5, 2025\nVector stores not being attached assistants when creating threads Bugs assistants ,  assistants-api ,  assistants-files ,  vector-store  |  | 1  | 159  | November 8, 2025\nError fetching connectors and all my custom connectors/apps gone ChatGPT chatgpt  |  | 1  | 121  | Nove