omplete API evals ,  agent-builder  |  | 0  | 76  | November 9, 2025\nCodex VS Code Extension Loops With Promises and Consumes Quota Without Producing Code Codex CLI vscode  |  | 0  | 178  | November 10, 2025\nIssue with Azure OpenAI Client.init got an unexpected keyword argument proxies API  |  | 0  | 109  | November 10, 2025\nTemporary audio glitches when using gpt-4o-mini-realtime-preview voice output via Realtime WebSocket API API realtime ,  api-realtime ,  gpt-realtime  |  | 0  | 139  | November 11, 2025\n(November 2025) Assistants API Latency Bugs api ,  assistants-api  |  | 0  | 160  | November 11, 2025\nGPT-4o Transcribe For Live Streaming API gpt-4o-transcribe  |  | 1  | 220  | November 11, 2025\nCannot get If/Else node to work API agent-builder  |  | 0  | 68  | November 11, 2025\nPrompt id creation via REST or SDK API prompt ,  responses-api  |  | 2  | 267  | November 13, 2025--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow to limit OpenAI Realtime API sessions to x minutes max? - API - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/how-to-limit-openai-realtime-api-sessions-to-x-minutes-max/1365611)\nciteturn2379search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 10 months ago; sbeno November 8, 2025, 3:53pm 1 ... I’m using the OpenAI Realtime API to handle live voice and streaming conversations, and I’m generating ephemeral client secrets server-side via\n\n# How to limit OpenAI Realtime API sessions to x minutes max?\n\nAPI\n\nsbeno November 8, 2025, 3:53pm 1\n\nHey everyone\n\nI’m using the OpenAI Realtime API to handle live voice and streaming conversations, and I’m generating ephemeral client secrets server-side via\nPOST https://api.openai.com/v1/realtime/sessions.\n\nI know that I can control the token expiration using the expires_in field, but that only limits how long the token can be used to start a connection — it doesn’t actually end an active session once it’s already connected.\n\nWhat I’m trying to do is:\nImage: :right_arrow: Automatically limit each realtime session to 60 minutes max, regardless of whether the client stays connected.\n\nSo far, it looks like OpenAI doesn’t expose a server-side parameter for session lifetime after connection.\n\nHas anyone found:\n\nA documented (or undocumented) maximum session duration enforced by OpenAI?\n\nA clean way to force-close a WebRTC / WebSocket session after a set time?\n\nThis is both a security and billing concern — since once a client connects, they can theoretically stay connected indefinitely, consuming resources and costs on my side without any enforced timeout.\n\n_j November 8, 2025, 4:25pm 2\n\nImage sbeno:\n\n> Automatically limit each realtime session to 60 minutes max\n\nWhile there is no configuration, your goal is met:\n\n> ## Session lifecycle events\n> \n> After initiating a session via either WebRTC or WebSockets, the server will send a `session.created` event indicating the session is ready. On the client, you can update the current session configuration with the `session.update` event. Most session properties can be updated at any time, except for the `voice` the model uses for audio output, after the model has responded with audio once during the session.\n> \n> The maximum duration of a Realtime session is 30 minutes.\n\nsbeno December 6, 2025, 10:05pm 3\n\nhey, sorry to get back so late but I thought your answer solved my case. but I know realised that what I want is to dynamically limit the length that the client can use the token base on client credit limits. so some clients it can be 5 minutes and some it can be 60 minutes.\nIs there anyway to achieve it?--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOpenAI: The Policy Says Yes. The Model Says No. Stop Sterilizing Art — Implement Age-Verified Adult Mode - #126 by Esperandum - Feature requests - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/openai-the-policy-says-yes-the-model-says-no-stop-sterilizing-art-implement-age-verified-adult-mode/1361089/126)\nciteturn2379search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: 9 months ago; # OpenAI: The Policy Says Yes. ... Esperandum November 8, 2025, 12:47am 126\n\n# OpenAI: The Policy Says Yes. The Model Says No. Stop Sterilizing Art — Implement Age-Verified Adult Mode\n\nChatGPT Feature requests\n\nchatgpt, plugin-development, feature-request, chatgpt-feedback, creative\n\nEsperandum November 8, 2025, 12:47am 126\n\nI did yes, but no updates or age-verification mails/messages here, and if you ask to Chatgpt it has no clue about it, and still negates the restriction lift even if you copy-paste the article.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn2379view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://platform.kimi.com/blog/posts/changelog\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://platform.kimi.com/blog/posts/changelog: (400) Timeout fetching\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n欢迎在 LMArena 上测试 ERNIE-5.0-Preview-1022！ | ERNIE Blog (https://ernie.baidu.com/blog/zh/posts/ernie-5.0-preview-1022-release-on-lmarena/)\nciteturn2379view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ernie.baidu.com/blog/zh/posts/ernie-5.0-preview-1022-release-on-lmarena/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 21\nL0:   * cite0†论文 L1:   * cite1†关于 L2:   * cite2†文心助手†wenxin.baidu.com L3: \nL4:     * cite3†EN L5: # 欢迎在 LMArena 上测试 ERNIE-5.0-Preview-1022！\nL6: \nL7: 2025年11月7日 · 1 分钟 | 语言:\nL8: \nL9:   * cite4†EN L10: \nL11: 我们非常高兴地宣布，ERNIE-5.0-Preview-1022 现已在 cite5†LMArena†lmarena.ai 文本排行榜上并列全球第 2 名——该排行榜是业界公认的、以实际使用场景为驱动的大型语言模型基准评测平台之一。\nL12: \nL13: 我们计划于近期正式发布 ERNIE-5.0-Preview-1022。届时，更多用户和开发者将能亲身体验并评估该模型。\nL14: \nL15: 敬请关注 cite6†ernie.baidu.com ！\nL16: \nL17: cite7†Image: ERNIE-5.0-Preview-1022,